[
    {
        "content": "<p>The regular elements of a (complete) Heyting algebra form a (complete) Boolean algebra, via the Galois connection induced by double negation. In mathlib, <code>BooleanAlgebra (Regular α)</code> is defined in this way: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs//Mathlib/Order/Heyting/Regular.html#Heyting.Regular.instBooleanAlgebra\">Heyting.Regular.instBooleanAlgebra</a>.</p>\n<p>I want to extend this to the complete lattice. That is, assuming <code>Order.Frame α</code>, I want to obtain <code>CompleteBooleanAlgebra (Regular α)</code>. This can in fact be obtained using <code>gi.liftCompleteLattice</code>, but that definition conflicts with <code>Heyting.Regular.lattice</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">GaloisConnection</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Heyting</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteBooleanAlgebra</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Frame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Heyting</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">completelattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CompleteLattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">gi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">liftCompleteLattice</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">boolean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BooleanAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CompleteBooleanAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inf_compl_le_bot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BooleanAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inf_compl_le_bot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">Type mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  BooleanAlgebra.inf_compl_le_bot x</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">has type</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  x ⊓ xᶜ ≤ @Bot.bot (Regular α) boolean.toBot</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  x ⊓ xᶜ ≤ @Bot.bot (Regular α) completelattice.toBot</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What is the appropriate way to deal with this?</p>",
        "id": 583434496,
        "sender_full_name": "Palalansoukî",
        "timestamp": 1775213258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Try something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">completelattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CompleteLattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">__</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Regular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">__</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">liftCompleteLattice</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583434665,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1775213335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, I didn't know that pattern.</p>",
